  "intentionalChanges": [
    "Stripe becomes the sole selectable/bound billing provider for all phone countries and obsolete/unknown configuration values.",
    "Both retired API clients, callbacks, runtime roots, routes, credentials examples, provider-specific tests and legacy live E2E script are removed; generated retired modules are cleaned.",
    "Billing presentation uses Stripe secure links consistently, including absent commercial metadata; old multi-provider price/name/fallback branches removed.",
    "Returned subscription write errors stop welcome messages instead of announcing success.",
    "Uncertain/unclassified welcome-text failures never replay via template; only owned KapsoValidationError with explicit 400/404/422 rejection permits that fallback.",
    "Stripe cancellation replaces the Mercado Pago adapter. Missing key, unsupported legacy ID, transport/parse/HTTP error or unconfirmed exact ID/canceled status blocks local update and confirmation.",
    "Payment-reference handling now recognizes generic checkout/buy/pay/subscription URLs without named retired providers, retaining informational treatment of old conversation links."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is required server-side for real remote cancellation; only synthetic credentials/transport were used here. No live keys read or configured.",
    "The legacy mp_preapproval_id field and compatibility persistence functions remain to preserve database/history; no rows or schema objects are deleted/renamed. Schema.sql changed only one explanatory comment.",
    "Historical migration evidence/docs retain prior provider facts; retirement supersedes those active-runtime descriptions without rewriting past results.",
    "No real existing vendor subscription, payment, channel, message or database record is changed; no deploy or external account cleanup.",
    "Stripe callback keeps previous signed-event/status/date/payload mapping and immediate ACK. It does not introduce event-ID deduplication, a durable webhook queue, full payment-state reconciliation or cross-service transaction receipts.",
    "Provider receipt validation and lease/write fences in Kapso are preserved. Other WhatsApp payload builders, ingress and jobs remain JS and require later migration.",
    "Billing row/query ports are consumed structural shapes and type-only boundaries, not universal SDK declaration conformance or new ownership authorization.",
    "Background memory remains best-effort process-local work; capture binds embedding scope at enqueue, not a new durable queue or inherited operational turn lease.",
    "After remote cancellation succeeds, local persistence may still fail; no automatic replay or atomic cross-service guarantee is introduced.",
    "Node22 uses three new synthetic billing SDK requests, prior SDK checks, two synthetic Kapso sends and one synthetic Stripe cancellation plus three AI requests; application storage/RPC counters and external HTTP effects zero. Not full server boot.",
    "No dependency, reminder-scheduler behavior, AI provider/model configuration, V2 activation or unsolicited commit."
  ]
}
